Subject: [PATCH] ecmcExampleTop: order _LIBS dependents before dependencies

The example IOC lists its libraries as:

    ecmcIoc_LIBS += asyn
    ecmcIoc_LIBS += ecmc
    ecmcIoc_LIBS += motor
    ecmcIoc_LIBS += exprtkSupport

EPICS emits `_LIBS` in the order given, so the link line reads
`-lasyn -lecmc -lmotor -lexprtkSupport`.  That is backwards.

A static archive only contributes the symbols already demanded by something
to its left.  `libecmc.a` needs `asynPortDriver`, but `libasyn.a` is scanned
before anything wants it, contributes nothing, and is discarded:

    libecmc.a(ecmcAsynPortDriver.o): undefined reference to
      `asynPortDriver::asynPortDriver(char const*, int, int, int, int, int, int, int)'
    libecmc.a(ecmcAsynPortDriver.o): undefined reference to
      `asynPortDriver::drvUserCreate(...)'
    ... and `typeinfo for asynPortDriver'

Note it is undefined references, not `cannot find -lasyn`.  The linker found
the library; it looked at it too early.

Reordering so dependents precede dependencies -- ecmc needs asyn, motor needs
asyn, so asyn goes last -- is correct under both linking modes.  It is not a
static-only workaround.

This is latent upstream.  Shared libraries record their own dependencies in
DT_NEEDED, so the runtime loader repairs bad ordering and nobody notices.  Only
a site building with `STATIC_BUILD=YES` -- as PCDS does -- ever sees it.

Worth reporting upstream: the ordering is wrong regardless of how any
particular site links.

Applies to: ecmc v11.0.8
Verified on: EPICS base R7.0.3.1-2.0, STATIC_BUILD=YES, rhel9-x86_64
---
 ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile b/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile
--- a/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile
+++ b/ecmcExampleTop/ecmcIocApp/src/Makefile
@@ -44,7 +44,11 @@
 ecmcIoc_DBD += motorSupport.dbd

 # Add all the support libraries needed by this IOC
-ecmcIoc_LIBS += asyn
+# Order matters: a static archive contributes only the symbols already
+# demanded to its left, so dependents must precede dependencies.  ecmc needs
+# asyn and motor needs asyn, so asyn goes last.  Harmless when linking
+# shared, required when linking static.
 ecmcIoc_LIBS += ecmc
 ecmcIoc_LIBS += motor
 ecmcIoc_LIBS += exprtkSupport
+ecmcIoc_LIBS += asyn
